       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day, which is twice the usual maximum for metformin. The maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. At that dose the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity goes up substantially.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day, the max for immediate-release.\n- **1700 mg/day in divided doses**, for example 850 mg twice daily.\n- **Another dose**, such as 500 mg or 1000 mg.\n\nTell me which dose you want and I'll enter it right away. If 1700 mg three times daily is what you intended, tell me that, and I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed the dose."
